From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 12:15:48 -0400
Subject: round: quieter defaults, a behaviour step, ten backlog items, the
 address band

The owner's pass on beta 13 (2026-10-11).

Auto-archive is Never by default (it was 12 hours), with a 7-day choice;
the welcome flow gains a sixth step that asks how idle tabs archive, how
the sidebar closes and whether a Space sleeps, Never preselected, and its
engines show their own marks instead of the globe (S-77).

Ten items: the page flush against the window (S-124); the sidebar edge's
bar and double click to the default width (S-123); mute and picture in
picture by key (S-122); folder verbs and a collapsed folder's count
(S-120), with the folder's rows drawn in the folder's order; a pin's home
edited by hand and a middle click sending a pin home (S-121); clearing a
site's cookies and reloading (S-119); Close Duplicate Tabs, a middle click
on the sidebar's ground opening the bar and a switch for the link address
on hover (S-125); inline completion in the command bar (S-108); Undo after
closing tabs, with a setting (S-97).

The address row's hover band starts at the chip and the address no longer
paints a second coat over it (toolbar T34), and toasts sit in the page
under the row instead of half over it (toolbar T35).

Why: the owner asked for nothing destructive by default and for ten small
backlog items built together; the faults found while building and using
them are fixed here, each with its behaviour id and a test.
Removable when: never; these are Stedding's own behaviours.
